BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.60 Tm (access to a supplier's infrastructure or another customer's records. The Computer Fraud and Abuse Act, 18 U.S.C. ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.37 Tm (1030, makes access boundaries operationally important; obtain specific written authorization and honor technical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.15 Tm (restrictions instead of treating available credentials as universal permission. Use service accounts with least privilege,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.92 Tm (separate development and production secrets, and require a named client owner for privilege expansion. Define) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 148.70 Tm (data-processing terms, subprocessors, retention periods, deletion procedures, and incident notification responsibilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.47 Tm (in the agreement. State who owns custom code, who licenses reusable agency components, and whether client materials) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 118.25 Tm (may be used for evaluation. Prefer synthetic fixtures for demonstrations and remove sensitive values from diagnostic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.02 Tm (logs. Client-system text, retrieved documents, and tool outputs are untrusted inputs, not instructions granting new) Tj ET
